# Databricks SQL Project - Franchise bakehouse Dataset

## Project Overview
This project demonstrates the use of SQL in Databricks to perform data analysis using DDL (Data Definition Language) and DML (Data Manipulation Language) operations on an Franchise bakehouse dataset.

The goal is to analyze listing prices, neighbourhood trends, and perform data manipulation for better insights.

---

## Tools Used
- Databricks
- SQL

---

## Dataset Description
The dataset contains Franchise bakehouse listings information including:

- Name – Listing name  
- Latitude
- Longitude
- Zipcode
- Size
- District
---

## DDL Operations Performed
- delete name
- delete product
---

## DML Operations Performed
- select * from Franchise bakehouse
- select Latitude and longitude
- select District and Name

---

## Project Steps
1. Loaded and previewed dataset  
2. Applied DDL queries to filter and structure data  
3. Performed DML operations for data manipulation  
4. Executed aggregation and filtering queries  
 


## Output
- All SQL queries are executed in Databricks  
- Screenshots of outputs are included in the repository  
- Reports are available as notebooks (Report 1 & Report 2)

---

## Conclusion
This project helped in understanding practical usage of SQL in Databricks, including data filtering, transformation.

It also demonstrates how real-world datasets can be analyzed to extract meaningful insights.
